2026-11-13T03:14:21.2024429Z # LexMachina — Query Map MVP
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2024696Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2024879Z Status: CANONICAL PRODUCT TARGET
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2025260Z Date: 2026-10-11
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2025417Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2025512Z ## 1. Product purpose
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2025640Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2026134Z LexMachina is a legal research interface, not a project to discover one universal geometry of all Swiss case law.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2026766Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2027058Z The user asks a legal research question. LexMachina must return:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2027497Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2027644Z 1. a sourced AI answer;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2028071Z 2. the relevant cases used to support that answer;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2028673Z 3. a visual map of the broader retrieved jurisprudence;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2029727Z 4. an explicit adversarial search for cases that contradict, limit, distinguish, or create exceptions to the provisional answer.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2030326Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2031072Z The visual map exists to help a jurist see structure that a ranked text list can hide: minority lines, isolated cases, alternative doctrinal branches, and unexpected bridges between groups.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2031687Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2031785Z ## 2. Core product loop
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2031918Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2032009Z For a query Q:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2032133Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2032239Z 1. Retrieve broadly from OpenCaseLaw.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2032577Z 2. Expand around strong candidates using citations where useful.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2032930Z 3. Preserve a high-recall candidate pool.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2033451Z 4. Rank / filter to a tractable map set (target: 100–300 decisions for the first MVP).
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2033966Z 5. Independently search for contrary / limiting / distinguishing authorities.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2034678Z 6. Build a query-specific similarity / relation graph.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2035054Z 7. Cluster and project that graph into an interactive map.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2035413Z 8. Generate concise cluster labels with provenance.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2035733Z 9. Produce a sourced AI answer.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2036089Z 10. Let the user inspect any decision, cluster, relation, or contrary authority.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2036382Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2036617Z The same decision may occupy a different position for a different query. This is expected.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2036950Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037029Z ## 3. Data source
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037151Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037341Z Primary Swiss public source: OpenCaseLaw public REST/MCP infrastructure.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037609Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037696Z Requirements:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2037893Z - no paid API key;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2038138Z - no login dependency for core public endpoints;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2039946Z - cache retrieved records locally for reproducibility;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2040428Z - preserve source URLs / decision IDs;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2040735Z - fail gracefully if the remote service is unavailable;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2041267Z - do not rebuild OpenCaseLaw's national corpus or citation graph unless a product-critical capability is missing.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2041663Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2042086Z The legacy 174k corpus and its artifacts remain preserved as research evidence and optional fallback/test data, but are no longer the critical path.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2042577Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2042671Z ## 4. Owner-time invariant
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2042808Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2043006Z The scarce resource is **the repository owner's attention**, not agent compute.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2043282Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2043643Z For development and testing, the canonical path must work without requiring the owner to buy or provision paid inference. Prefer:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2044404Z - OpenCaseLaw public API / MCP;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2044684Z - OpenCode free models / healthy free fallbacks;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2044990Z - locally runnable open-source models;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2045271Z - open-source Python/JS libraries;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2045535Z - existing repository artifacts.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2045691Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2046406Z This is a development/test constraint, NOT a permanent product architecture constraint. A future production service may use paid or hosted LLM/embedding/reranking infrastructure if that improves the product and has a viable business case.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2047207Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2047573Z The factory must not trade away product quality or create needless engineering solely to avoid hypothetical future inference cost.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2048017Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2048104Z Owner-attention rules:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2048345Z - technical failures auto-retry or reroute;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2048732Z - implementation choices inside the canonical mission are made autonomously;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2049277Z - do not ask the owner to choose libraries, embeddings, layouts, thresholds, or repair strategies;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2049769Z - do not ask for manual data preparation that agents can perform;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2050599Z - surface a human gate only when a clickable product is ready for judgment, or when an unavoidable product/business/legal/external-access choice genuinely requires the owner.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2051173Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2051277Z ## 5. Retrieval-first doctrine
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2051435Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2051591Z A visualizer cannot reveal a case that retrieval never found.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2051837Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2052021Z Therefore the first product metric is retrieval coverage, not map beauty.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2052307Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2052441Z The pipeline should combine free techniques as useful:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2052773Z - OpenCaseLaw lexical / filtered search;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2053047Z - query expansion in DE/FR/IT;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2053295Z - exact norm / citation retrieval;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2053574Z - citation-neighborhood expansion;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2053832Z - TF-IDF / BM25 reranking;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2054276Z - existing accepted LexMachina representations where they help;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2054856Z - optional open-source multilingual embeddings if they improve retrieval on frozen tests without paid inference.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2055267Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2055458Z Do not build a new universal 174k embedding space merely to satisfy this MVP.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2055747Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2055871Z ## 6. Adversarial / counter-authority pass
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2056054Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2056412Z After drafting a provisional answer, run an independent retrieval pass whose instruction is to find authorities that could:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2056835Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2056951Z - contradict the provisional conclusion;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2057211Z - narrow it;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2057425Z - distinguish the factual/legal situation;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2057692Z - reveal an exception;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2058007Z - show a minority or older line;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2058263Z - expose a language-specific branch;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2058528Z - undermine the apparent consensus.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2058697Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2058926Z These cases must be retained in the map even when their initial relevance score is lower.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2059235Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2059790Z The UI must distinguish "supporting", "limiting", "contrary/exception", and "unclassified" only when the classification is actually supported. Uncertain classifications must remain uncertain.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2060417Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2060513Z ## 7. Query-specific map
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2060660Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2060973Z The map is generated from the retrieved set, not from a claim that all Swiss cases possess one canonical global position.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2061378Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2061460Z Minimum map semantics:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2061674Z - point = decision;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2061987Z - spatial proximity = query-conditioned similarity / relation strength;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2062369Z - cluster = locally coherent result group;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2062697Z - visible outliers = isolated or weakly connected decisions;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2063054Z - citation/relation edges available on selection;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2063371Z - counter-authorities visually discoverable;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2063676Z - cluster labels explain why the group exists.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2063870Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2064488Z 2D or 3D is an implementation choice. 3D is useful only if it increases comprehension. A beautiful 3D point cloud with no readable legal structure fails.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2064986Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065066Z ## 8. AI answer
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065189Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065307Z The AI answer and the map are complementary.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065493Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065587Z Answer requirements:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2065807Z - answer the legal question;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2066088Z - cite decisions actually retrieved from the source;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2066415Z - separate strong propositions from uncertainty;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2066930Z - mention material counter-authorities / exceptions surfaced by the adversarial pass;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2067451Z - provide links / identifiers so the user can inspect the underlying decision.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2067739Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2067996Z The map must remain available after the answer so the user can independently audit what the AI said.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068348Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068429Z ## 9. MVP UI
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068535Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068631Z One page is enough.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068753Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2068838Z Required:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2069029Z - search / question input;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2069263Z - sourced answer panel;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2069480Z - interactive map;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2069683Z - result count;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2069878Z - cluster labels;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2070108Z - decision detail panel;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2070363Z - toggle / emphasis for counter-authorities;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2070641Z - relation edges on selection;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2070884Z - search within current result set;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071129Z - reset / fit view.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071254Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071347Z Nice-to-have, not MVP blockers:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071578Z - 3D terrain;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071764Z - animation;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2071966Z - full corpus browse mode;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2072188Z - custom corpus import;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2072401Z - multiple legal views.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2072528Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2072627Z ## 9A. Performance architecture
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2072779Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2073272Z Performance is part of the product hypothesis. A visually auditable system that feels materially slower than ordinary legal search will fail even if its clusters are good.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2073846Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2073933Z ### Progressive pipeline
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2074398Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2074529Z Do NOT serialize the whole query path behind the LLM.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2074746Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2074834Z Preferred flow:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2075075Z 1. normalize query + check persistent cache;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2075441Z 2. run broad OpenCaseLaw search/query variants with bounded concurrency;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2075859Z 3. deduplicate and return the first ranked candidate set;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2076232Z 4. compute a fast initial query-specific map and render it;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2076727Z 5. in parallel, fetch richer text/structure only for the evidence subset needed for answer generation;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2077178Z 6. stream/generate the sourced answer;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2077624Z 7. run the adversarial/counter-authority pass in parallel or immediately after the provisional answer;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2078188Z 8. incrementally update the map/statuses when additional authorities are found.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2078482Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2078712Z The initial map MUST NOT wait for completion of the generative answer or adversarial pass.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2079036Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2079130Z ### Hot-path constraints
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2079268Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2079570Z - Query-specific mode must not initialize/load the legacy 174k global-map representations at server startup.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2080079Z - Legacy artifacts are lazy/optional fallback only.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2081169Z - Do not fetch full text for all 100–300 mapped cases before first render. Use search/regeste/snippet metadata for broad-map geometry; lazily fetch full decision/structure for the smaller answer-evidence set and clicked cases.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2082070Z - Deduplicate before expensive full-text/network/LLM work.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2082523Z - Use bounded concurrent remote calls while respecting OpenCaseLaw pacing/rate limits.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2083144Z - Persist query/result/source caches to disk so repeated queries and test fixtures avoid repeated network work.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2083885Z - Separate the broad map pool from the answer context. The LLM should receive a selected evidence pack, not 300 complete judgments.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2084810Z - Cache expensive map geometry by query + retrieval/config hash.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2085277Z - Do not recompute unchanged clusters/projection merely because answer text changed.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2085588Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2085676Z ### MVP latency budgets
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2085817Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2085948Z These are engineering targets, not scientific claims:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2086403Z - lightweight server startup: target < 3 s excluding first-time local model download/start;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2086854Z - cached query to initial map: target < 1 s;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2087644Z - upstream search latency is external (OpenCaseLaw currently documents roughly 5–15 s typical search latency); measure it separately;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2088425Z - after the first OpenCaseLaw result page arrives, local normalize/rerank/geometry/render overhead: target < 1.5 s;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2089281Z - first map may render from the first ~50–100 results; expand incrementally toward ~100–300 without clearing/freezing the UI;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2089955Z - local clustering/projection for ~100–300 decisions: target < 2 s;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2090411Z - decision click/detail from already fetched data: target < 150 ms locally;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2090899Z - answer generation should stream or expose progress rather than block the map;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2091415Z - counter-authority updates may arrive later, but must not freeze the interface.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2091708Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2092351Z Record measured p50/p95-like timings for frozen fixtures/live smoke tests where practical. If UMAP/Leiden or another sophisticated method violates the budget without measurable UX gain, fall back to the simpler method.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2093064Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2093168Z ### Memory/startup discipline
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2093328Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2093903Z The query-map MVP should run without loading corpus-scale matrices into RAM. Existing 174k assets are reusable research components but are not allowed on the default hot path.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2094606Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2094712Z ## 10. Reuse from existing LexMachina
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2094887Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2094991Z Reuse only when it reduces time-to-test:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2095278Z - existing TF-IDF / lexical tooling;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2095540Z - multilingual robustness tests;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2095795Z - clustering / hierarchy code;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2096038Z - WebGL / Canvas rendering;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2096262Z - LOD / culling;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2096488Z - decision detail / navigation components;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2096779Z - benchmark discipline and negative results.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2096972Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2097058Z Do NOT block the MVP on:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2097359Z - global 174k id→cluster alignment;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2097625Z - global citation-graph reconstruction;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2097903Z - dense 174k embeddings;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2098132Z - universal fractal hierarchy;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2098487Z - BGE/bger crosswalk work beyond what the new query pipeline actually needs.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2098766Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2098867Z ## 10A. Reuse-first inventory
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2099011Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2099369Z The product pivot does **not** invalidate the month of prior LexMachina work. Reuse existing implementation before replacing it.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2099809Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2099930Z Known reusable assets on `lab/product` include:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2100458Z - `product/server.py`: threaded stdlib HTTP server, response cache, rate limiting, health/error patterns and API routing;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2101257Z - `product/static/index.html`: existing interactive WebGL/Canvas map UI, search/filter controls and decision/cluster interaction patterns;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2101964Z - `product/app/navigation.py`: navigation/search/decision/neighbor/citation API patterns;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2102470Z - `product/app/map_loader.py`: representation/map loading contracts;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2103063Z - existing clustering/projection tooling based on scikit-learn, NetworkX, igraph/Leiden and UMAP;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2103641Z - existing spatial-index, LOD/culling, proximity-explanation and import patterns;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2104374Z - accepted evaluation work on multilingual robustness, jurist preference, boilerplate resistance and deterministic benchmarking.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2104826Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2104906Z Reuse rule:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2105103Z 1. adapt before rewriting;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2105385Z 2. preserve historical artifacts and negative results;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2105983Z 3. if an old global-174k assumption blocks adaptation, isolate it behind a new query-bundle adapter rather than replacing the whole server/UI;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2106710Z 4. the preferred new abstraction is a `query_result_bundle` consumed by the existing product shell.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2107055Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2107185Z Suggested minimum `query_result_bundle` fields:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2107461Z - query;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2107673Z - generated_answer + cited decision IDs;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2107961Z - retrieval metadata/provenance;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2108202Z - decisions[];
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2108420Z - per-decision retrieval/rerank scores;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2108711Z - counter_authority_status with uncertainty;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2108989Z - cluster_id / cluster_label;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2109234Z - x/y (and optional z) projection;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2109485Z - typed relations/citations;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2109726Z - source URL / citation string.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2109883Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2109990Z ## 10B. Autonomous execution / anti-drift rule
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2110186Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2110528Z The MVP should not need another open-ended research program, but **there is no arbitrary limit on free autonomous agent cycles**.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2111025Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2111119Z Preferred milestone sequence:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2111661Z - first usable vertical slice: real OpenCaseLaw/cached query -> query_result_bundle -> source-linked clickable map using reused UI/server;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2112398Z - next: sourced generative answer + independent counter-authority pass integrated into that same UI;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2113022Z - then: autonomous fixes driven by evaluation until the product is ready for the human product gate.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2113367Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2114269Z Agents may iterate as long as they are making measurable progress. Repeated cycles with no executable delta must trigger autonomous diagnosis, rerouting or narrower implementation — not a request for owner intervention.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2115046Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2115158Z The relevant cost metric is owner attention:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2115520Z - zero owner involvement during routine implementation/debugging;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2115976Z - one owner checkpoint when a genuinely usable end-to-end product is ready;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2116536Z - additional owner involvement only for a true product decision that autonomous evidence cannot resolve.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2116896Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2116998Z ## 11. Automated evaluation
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2117142Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2117599Z Create a small frozen set of real Swiss legal research questions with known useful authorities and at least some known limiting / contrary authority where feasible.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2118138Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2118213Z Measure:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2118419Z - recall of known relevant authorities;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2118699Z - recall of known counter-authorities;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2118955Z - duplication rate;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2119172Z - language robustness;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2119387Z - source validity;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2119586Z - cluster stability;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2119784Z - latency;
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120013Z - deterministic reproducibility of cached runs.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120213Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120360Z Do not pretend these automated tests prove UX usefulness.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120585Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120671Z ## 12. Human product gate
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2120895Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2121257Z The MVP earns further investment only if a jurist can use it on real research questions and answer YES to at least two of the following:
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2121704Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2122003Z 1. The map exposed a relevant branch / case / exception that was less visible in the ranked list or AI answer.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2122550Z 2. The map made the structure of the jurisprudence easier to understand.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2123064Z 3. The map increased confidence that contrary authority had not simply been hidden by the answer.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2123616Z 4. The combined answer + map was preferable to a conventional answer + result list.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2123914Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2124431Z If this does not happen on a small set of real research tasks, STOP investing in LexMachina as a standalone product.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2124832Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2124938Z ## 13. Immediate implementation order
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2125119Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2125303Z ### Milestone A — end-to-end free query pipeline
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2125814Z OpenCaseLaw query → cached candidate set → free reranking → AI answer → JSON result bundle.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2126138Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2126284Z ### Milestone B — adversarial retrieval
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2126827Z Independent counter-authority search → merge/deduplicate → classify conservatively → expose in result bundle.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2127220Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2127364Z ### Milestone C — clickable query map
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2127873Z 100–300 decisions → similarity/relation graph → clusters → projection → interactive browser UI.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2128222Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2128352Z ### Milestone D — product evaluation
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2129036Z Frozen benchmark queries + human test. Only after this gate should the factory spend effort on more sophisticated geometry, 3D, dense embeddings, or large-scale custom infrastructure.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2129739Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2129830Z ## 14. Kill rule
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2129954Z 
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2130680Z If repeated autonomous work cannot produce a clickable end-to-end prototype without consuming repeated owner attention, record that as a failure of the autonomous-development approach and simplify/reroute before asking the owner to intervene.
2026-11-13T03:14:21.2131495Z 
