2026-11-13T03:16:01.9601151Z """The LEGACY product server's query API must work when it is launched the way
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9601807Z the README and the reports launch it.
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9602092Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9602261Z Why this exists
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9602654Z ---------------
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9603316Z Producer cycle 39646409851 changed ``product/server.py``'s import bootstrap
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9603940Z from
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9604275Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9604698Z     sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent))   # repository root
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9605296Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9605469Z to
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9605636Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9605853Z     sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent))           # product/ only
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9606165Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9606418Z and left it there.  The repository root is REQUIRED: ``product/query/bundle.py``
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9607009Z imports ``from product.query.counter_status import ...`` absolutely, and when
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9607561Z the server is started as ``python3 product/server.py`` the only entry on
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9608090Z ``sys.path`` is the script's own directory (``product/``), so the package
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9608625Z ``product`` is not importable at all.  Every ``/api/query/*`` endpoint then
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9609181Z dies with ``ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'product'`` and the HTTP
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9609747Z handler returns an empty 500 - the query-map product is unreachable through
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9610393Z this server.
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9610529Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9610762Z The defect is invisible to a test that only imports the pipeline from the
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9611309Z repository root (``pytest`` puts the root on ``sys.path``), which is why it
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9611870Z survived: the failure exists only in the SHIPPED LAUNCH COMMAND.  These tests
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9612447Z therefore spawn the real process, the way the browser and the operator do, and
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9612912Z drive it over a real socket.
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9613099Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9613200Z What is pinned here
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9613452Z -------------------
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9613856Z 1. ``python3 product/server.py <port> --query-mode`` answers ``/api/health``
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9614555Z    in query mode (no 174k corpus load): ``mode="query"``,
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9614971Z    ``corpus_decisions=0``, ``query_pipeline="ready"``;
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9615413Z 2. ``/api/query/map?...&mode=fixture`` returns HTTP 200 and a real
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9615897Z    ``query_result_bundle`` with decisions, clusters and coordinates
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9616400Z    (the regression: this is the call that used to die on the import);
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9616915Z 3. ``/api/query/answer?...&mode=fixture`` returns HTTP 200 and an answer;
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9617458Z 4. the retrieval mode is part of the response cache key, so a fixture answer
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9617976Z    can never be served for a live request (observed through
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9618354Z    ``/api/cache/stats``);
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9618740Z 5. ``/static/<file>`` serves the shipped assets with the right content type,
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9619266Z    including ``.html`` (serving the page as ``text/css`` would break it in a
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9619861Z    browser), and never escapes ``product/static/``.
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9620111Z 
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9620358Z The tests are offline and deterministic: fixture retrieval, fixture generation,
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9620837Z no outbound network, no paid inference.
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9621138Z """
2026-11-13T03:16:01.9621374Z from __future__ import annotations
